{
  "version": 1,
  "_note": "MARK GEOMETRY - datum to coordinate, exactly. Three renderers draw pixels three ways, so the corpus asserts the MAPPING and lets the painting differ. The degenerate cases are the point: a pie of a single slice must report itself FULL so a renderer draws a circle instead of a 360-degree arc path that collapses to nothing (the bug every SVG pie ships once), a pie whose values sum to zero is EMPTY rather than a division by zero, a candle whose open equals its close is FLAT and still gets a minimum body so the doji is visible, and the last heatmap bin owns its own upper edge instead of spilling into a phantom bin+1. Bubble radius interpolates AREA, not radius, because the eye reads area.",
